1
00:00:14,723 --> 00:00:18,351
I got married when I was quite young.

2
00:00:19,352 --> 00:00:23,648
My husband and I met
right after we graduated high school.

3
00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:25,525
I was just starting a new job.

4
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:28,194
<i>After we were married,</i>

5
00:00:28,778 --> 00:00:29,988
<i>I quit working,</i>

6
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:32,741
<i>and I've been a housewife ever since.</i>

7
00:00:33,241 --> 00:00:35,660
We were sadly never blessed with children,

8
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:37,871
so it's just been the two of us here.

9
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:40,749
This is us in Paris.

10
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:43,293
<i>He took me when we were newlyweds.</i>

11
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:45,253
<i>That's my fondest memory.</i>

12
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:48,048
- Blood pressure?
- No change.

13
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:51,384
- Could you give us some space, please?
- Sorry, yeah.

14
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:55,180
<i>I received my cancer diagnosis first, but</i>

15
00:00:56,639 --> 00:00:59,934
<i>it was my husband</i>
<i>who passed away before me.</i>

16
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,313
<i>I was alone.</i>

17
00:01:04,022 --> 00:01:05,482
My friends all said,

18
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:10,904
"How nice. You can finally live your life.
You're free to do anything you want."

19
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:16,326
But if I'm being honest,
I didn't know what to do. I was lost.

20
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:18,036
<i>It's an emergency.</i>

21
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:20,121
There just aren't enough doctors.

22
00:01:20,205 --> 00:01:22,624
And the documentary's
keeping the director busy.

23
00:01:22,707 --> 00:01:24,876
So we ask for help from the dark side.

24
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:27,504
Whoa! Like Mr. Spot Remover?
Or Ms. Backlash?

25
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:30,715
Mr. Spot Remover's one thing,
Ms. Backlash is something else.

26
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:32,967
We can't have people
finding out she works here.

27
00:01:33,051 --> 00:01:35,220
- It would ruin us.
- We don't have any other choice.

28
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:39,724
When did I become interested
in cosmetic surgery?

29
00:01:39,808 --> 00:01:41,559
When I saw it on TV.

30
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:46,022
Uh, Dr. Tohyama's father had that program.

31
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:48,817
They used to play it on,
uh, Tuesday nights.

32
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,527
I don't recall the name though.

33
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:51,778
<i>Beauty Revolution.</i>

34
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:54,906
That's it, yes.
I loved it. I watched it all the time.

35
00:01:54,989 --> 00:01:57,617
Now it's time to see how our guest
has been transformed.

36
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:58,576
Come on out!

37
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,162
It's completely changed my life.

38
00:02:04,999 --> 00:02:06,459
Oh, she looks like a star!

39
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:09,504
Incredible. Another amazing
transformation this week.

40
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:12,382
Just look at her!
Impressive as ever, Dr. Tohyama.

41
00:02:12,465 --> 00:02:13,967
I'd call this another success.

42
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:17,262
The Hand of God can fix it all.

43
00:02:17,762 --> 00:02:20,723
"The Hand of God can fix it all."

44
00:02:22,016 --> 00:02:23,768
I loved that show.

45
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:25,353
Watched it every week.

46
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:26,729
- Oh yeah.
- Mm.

47
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:30,567
I thought if I were to get
that kind of surgery,

48
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:34,070
I'd put myself
in Dr. Tohyama's capable hands.

49
00:02:34,154 --> 00:02:35,572
And what…

50
00:02:35,655 --> 00:02:39,159
What if your husband were still with us?
Would you still get the operation?

51
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:40,451
I don't know…

52
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:42,245
Probably not.

53
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:44,164
Because he'd be against it?

54
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:46,416
Mm, no, it's nothing like that.

55
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:47,709
No, not at all.

56
00:02:47,792 --> 00:02:50,503
It's more that, before he passed away,

57
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:53,423
I had never thought
to do anything for myself.

58
00:02:53,506 --> 00:02:57,302
So this surgery is, uh,
something you're doing for yourself?

59
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:01,931
Yes.

60
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:58,738
DOCTOR TANUMA

61
00:03:58,821 --> 00:04:01,574
- I already said that it's Numata.
- I know.

62
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:03,576
We want you to work under an alias.

63
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:07,121
We don't have enough doctors,
and we want you taking on new clients.

64
00:04:08,331 --> 00:04:10,500
- No.
- You don't have to worry.

65
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,711
You'll be supported by Ms. Todoroki
every step of the way.

66
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:20,093
<i>Mr. Ohashi, I understand</i>

67
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:23,054
that you've requested
to speak with one of our doctors.

68
00:04:23,137 --> 00:04:25,056
What would you like to discuss today?

69
00:04:25,556 --> 00:04:26,474
Yeah.

70
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:28,434
It's, uh…

71
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:30,311
It's my palm lines.

72
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:31,688
His palm lines?

73
00:04:31,771 --> 00:04:34,357
Thing is, I was born
with some serious bad luck.

74
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,819
Work's bad, but my relationships
are even worse.

75
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:41,531
And my… Well, my mom thinks
it's all because of my palm lines.

76
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:43,241
Yeah. You can see.

77
00:04:43,324 --> 00:04:47,412
Here, my fate line,
my sun line, and my wealth line,

78
00:04:47,495 --> 00:04:49,580
are all quite faint,
which indicates weakness.

79
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:53,042
And my mother thinks that if those three
were connected to my Hao line,

80
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:54,294
my luck would improve!

81
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:55,378
So… yeah.

82
00:04:55,461 --> 00:04:57,297
SCULPTING THE FUTURE

83
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:58,881
I see. Well, first, let me say,

84
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:01,968
the palm has
a high concentration of nerve endings.

85
00:05:02,051 --> 00:05:04,387
A careless incision
could cause scar contracture,

86
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:06,139
which could then become a source of pain.

87
00:05:06,222 --> 00:05:07,265
Wait. I'd feel pain?

88
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:08,558
Not to mention, sir,

89
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:11,311
if changing the lines on your palm
could change your fate,

90
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:13,604
don't you think
everyone would be getting it done?

91
00:05:13,688 --> 00:05:15,273
Well, that's, um…

92
00:05:15,773 --> 00:05:17,984
- Um, so you're saying the Hao line is--
- Sir!

93
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:19,861
We'll do it for you.

94
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:23,489
I've heard that, in China,
the procedure has become quite the hit.

95
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:29,412
We'd be very pleased to help. I can't wait
to see how your future will change.

96
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:33,458
Really? Thank you, miss.

97
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:36,419
Marry me?

98
00:05:38,796 --> 00:05:39,922
Ms. Todoroki!

99
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:41,966
I don't understand
why you booked the procedure

100
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:43,301
despite my professional opinion.

101
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:45,887
Because there was no reason to refuse it.
It can be done.

102
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:47,221
- Hang on a second.
- Also…

103
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:51,351
You need to stop mocking
your patients' concerns.

104
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:52,268
Mocking?

105
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:54,771
People come here
with problems they want solved.

106
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:57,023
Problems they've worried about.
And we help.

107
00:05:57,523 --> 00:06:00,068
We don't look down on our patients
at this clinic.

108
00:06:00,651 --> 00:06:01,652
Hm.

109
00:06:05,656 --> 00:06:07,825
<i>She actually took on the palm surgery?</i>

110
00:06:07,909 --> 00:06:11,162
But when did we start offering
that kind of treatment here?

111
00:06:11,245 --> 00:06:12,538
Don't worry.

112
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:15,625
The point of cosmetic surgery
is the customer's satisfaction.

113
00:06:16,125 --> 00:06:18,002
Though I doubt
he'll walk out with better luck.

114
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:21,547
Ah, so Dr. Backlash
might have to take another loss?

115
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:24,717
- Ms. Kato wants surgery today?
- Yes. She was insistent.

116
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:27,804
- Let's prepare Room B then.
- Of course.

117
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:29,180
Mm. It's payback.

118
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:32,392
Ms. Todoroki and Kanabun
were good friends, weren't they?

119
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:33,935
- Mm.
- Mm-hmm.

120
00:06:34,018 --> 00:06:36,396
What? False advertising?

121
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:38,648
Yeah. We'll need a full list of any ads

122
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:41,150
that use the phrase "The Hand of God"
so we can scrub them.

123
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:42,318
Hang on, wait.

124
00:06:42,944 --> 00:06:44,153
There must be some mistake.

125
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:48,908
We've been using it for years. My…
My dad coined it for his TV appearances.

126
00:06:48,991 --> 00:06:53,162
I know that. But in the eyes of the law,
you're not a deity. You're a human being.

127
00:06:53,746 --> 00:06:55,081
If a judge considers the phrase

128
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:58,042
to violate medical advertising guidelines,
we're cooked.

129
00:07:00,044 --> 00:07:01,879
Right, so who's stirring up trouble?

130
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:03,923
It would appear to be the MBC Group.

131
00:07:04,006 --> 00:07:05,133
SOTARO ANDO

132
00:07:05,216 --> 00:07:06,342
MBC Group? Ha!

133
00:07:06,426 --> 00:07:09,220
Their free surgeries scam
is making them millions.

134
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:13,224
- And they talk about ethics.
- Listen. We need to handle it.

135
00:07:13,307 --> 00:07:16,185
There are some things that can be done
and some that can't.

136
00:07:19,730 --> 00:07:21,899
<i>Are you struggling with something?</i>

137
00:07:23,484 --> 00:07:26,946
<i>Your new self begins right here.</i>

138
00:07:28,322 --> 00:07:31,242
<i>From dream to reality.</i>

139
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:33,953
<i>You can be reborn.</i>

140
00:07:35,246 --> 00:07:36,706
<i>The Hand of God</i>

141
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:38,332
<i>will change you.</i>

142
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:40,460
You wanna bet she's had surgery too?

143
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,462
Yeah, apparently not.

144
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:44,338
There's pictures of her
as a kid going around.

145
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:45,548
<i>…deserves beauty.</i>

146
00:07:46,048 --> 00:07:47,216
<i>Including you.</i>

147
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:49,260
Oh!

148
00:07:50,928 --> 00:07:52,138
What a gross commercial.

149
00:07:52,221 --> 00:07:54,557
It nearly ruins a perfectly good meal.

150
00:07:55,057 --> 00:07:57,351
This again? Your mother hates the idea.

151
00:07:57,435 --> 00:07:58,728
Plastic surgery.

152
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:02,398
When I told her I wanted some,
she practically divorced me.

153
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:04,275
What would you wanna get done, Dad?

154
00:08:04,358 --> 00:08:06,235
You'll never know.

155
00:08:07,695 --> 00:08:10,364
Of course. You shouldn't be
getting surgeries if you're not working.

156
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:12,241
- Yeah, yeah.
- Hey, I'm home!

157
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:13,451
- Oh, hi, Fumi.
- Hey.

158
00:08:13,951 --> 00:08:16,120
Oh, I'm starving…

159
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:18,331
What's with all the food?
What the heck's going on?

160
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:21,876
Ah, Takashi! I thought I told you
to cut back on all this stuff.

161
00:08:21,959 --> 00:08:24,629
Hey now, hang on. This is Macky's treat.

162
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:26,756
- Macky?
- Do we need more chopsticks?

163
00:08:28,132 --> 00:08:30,134
Uh, it's been a minute.

164
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:32,011
Please. My friends call me Macky.

165
00:08:36,098 --> 00:08:39,477
Look, I spent ages working on the broth,
so dig in, please!

166
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,270
- Dig in.
- Whoa, <i>chawanmushi!</i>

167
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:43,773
- It's <i>chawanmushi.</i>
- Sake?

168
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:45,608
- Let's do it!
- Hey.

169
00:08:49,028 --> 00:08:50,071
What?

170
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:52,031
What do you think you're doing here?

171
00:08:52,114 --> 00:08:54,200
I, um… It's <i>chawanmushi, </i>and I thought--

172
00:08:54,283 --> 00:08:55,993
Listen, Fumi. Hang on.

173
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:57,495
- Get out, go.
- Takeru is--

174
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:59,747
Who gave you
the right to walk in here? Huh?

175
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:01,040
- Hey!
- Sis!

176
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:04,961
You goddamn loan shark.
You're a parasite. Get the hell out!

177
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:08,214
Get out!

178
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:21,269
- Like this, man.
- Oh, sure, yeah.

179
00:09:24,772 --> 00:09:27,316
Good evening. May I have your name?

180
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:29,193
Is Director Ando available?

181
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:31,612
Yes. Just a moment please.

182
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:34,949
Takeru. Hey.

183
00:09:35,783 --> 00:09:36,826
What's going on?

184
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:38,744
I'm coming in.

185
00:09:40,538 --> 00:09:41,455
Huh?

186
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,002
Takeru!

187
00:09:46,085 --> 00:09:47,420
Unlock the door!

188
00:09:47,503 --> 00:09:49,130
Are you listening? What's wrong?

189
00:09:49,213 --> 00:09:51,007
- Why did you kick him out?
- What?

190
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:52,550
I invited him.

191
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:54,719
I owe him.

192
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:57,680
What's that mean?
You know what kind of man he is.

193
00:09:57,763 --> 00:09:59,724
Whatever. Just go away.

194
00:10:07,023 --> 00:10:08,858
You blew up at him.

195
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:12,862
You didn't even want to hear Macky out.
Of course Takeru was pissed.

196
00:10:12,945 --> 00:10:15,573
You've already forgotten
how shitty he's been to us?

197
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:19,493
No. But Macky's had a tough life,
too, you know.

198
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:22,788
He borrowed money from a loan shark
and wasn't able to pay him back,

199
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:25,082
so now he's got no choice
but to work as a debt collector.

200
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:27,043
Dunno why that should matter to me.

201
00:10:27,126 --> 00:10:29,962
Well, because maybe
Takeru's taken a shine to him.

202
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:32,673
Don't start with that, okay?
I'll take care of Takeru.

203
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:35,718
- But you gotta stay out of it.
- That's out of the question. No.

204
00:10:36,218 --> 00:10:39,138
- I gave birth to him. I can handle him.
- You had a C-section.

205
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:42,642
C-sections still hurt,
Miss High and Mighty.

206
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:44,602
I thought you were a doctor.
How do you not know?

207
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:47,146
Wait. Hang on a second.

208
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:49,607
Are you drinking?

209
00:10:49,690 --> 00:10:51,400
- Give me that!
- Stop, no.

210
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:52,693
Give me the drink.

211
00:10:55,571 --> 00:10:57,406
I'm not allowed green juice now?

212
00:10:57,907 --> 00:11:00,993
Stop sticking your nose in my business.

213
00:11:01,077 --> 00:11:01,952
Bitch.

214
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:04,955
Bitch?

215
00:11:07,792 --> 00:11:09,085
Ah.

216
00:11:09,585 --> 00:11:11,504
It's delicious. I love it.

217
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:14,965
Bitch?

218
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:18,594
I'm just trying to figure this out,
because it doesn't make any sense.

219
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:21,013
Why would the biggest chain in Japan

220
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:23,599
go after a clinic
with only three branches here?

221
00:11:23,683 --> 00:11:26,477
I don't get it.
There's no point, you know?

222
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,436
Listen, Rin.

223
00:11:27,937 --> 00:11:31,440
The fact is that Dr. Arata
made his name as The Hand of God.

224
00:11:31,524 --> 00:11:34,735
And I understand that makes it
an important phrase for Tohyama Clinic.

225
00:11:34,819 --> 00:11:36,570
And so?

226
00:11:36,654 --> 00:11:37,571
Rin,

227
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:40,950
I was Dr. Arata's top student.

228
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:43,077
I've watched him perform surgery.

229
00:11:43,577 --> 00:11:46,539
You don't have to tell me he's a genius.
I've seen it.

230
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:50,251
But that's Dr. Arata.

231
00:11:51,293 --> 00:11:53,754
Why would I believe
you are as good as him?

232
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:57,675
- I think you're pushing it.
- I'm his chosen successor.

233
00:11:58,509 --> 00:12:01,053
I don't remember
that privilege going to you,

234
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:03,347
Ando.

235
00:12:03,431 --> 00:12:06,392
Which is why he passed
the "Hand of God" title on to me.

236
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:10,062
All that says is that he wanted
to keep the name in the family.

237
00:12:11,021 --> 00:12:12,732
And that's not his style.

238
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:15,526
Sounds like something
a third-rate dictator would do.

239
00:12:16,152 --> 00:12:17,695
He'd never stoop so low.

240
00:12:18,654 --> 00:12:22,366
MBC was started for just that reason.

241
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:24,618
We're not getting anywhere.

242
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:27,705
We're clearly at a crossroad.

243
00:12:29,081 --> 00:12:31,167
Sorry for dropping in on you
like this. Excuse me.

244
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:32,752
Are the rumors true?

245
00:12:33,335 --> 00:12:35,379
That Dr. Arata is returning to practice?

246
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:39,300
- What?
- Yeah.

247
00:12:40,301 --> 00:12:44,430
I'm sure it's nothing, but I heard a rumor
he's looking for property in Tokyo.

248
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:46,891
Absolutely not.

249
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:48,350
Thought so.

250
00:12:49,143 --> 00:12:52,605
Coming back would just mean
putting you in a tough position.

251
00:13:05,409 --> 00:13:06,410
Give it back.

252
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:09,497
Give me back my silicone.

253
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:10,581
Give it back!

254
00:13:19,548 --> 00:13:22,009
Please don't come. I'm serious.

255
00:13:22,092 --> 00:13:23,427
Now hang on.

256
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:25,846
You understand I can't just not go.

257
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:27,640
Because I'm a board member.

258
00:13:27,723 --> 00:13:30,434
So what? I'm not going to school
if you show up.

259
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:32,353
What? What do you mean?

260
00:13:32,436 --> 00:13:35,356
Can we keep it down? It's my day off
and you guys have to argue first thing?

261
00:13:35,439 --> 00:13:37,483
Whatever. Just don't come!

262
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:42,988
- At least he's still in school.
- What?

263
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:46,325
This is all because of you
and your big mouth. You know that?

264
00:13:46,992 --> 00:13:48,911
What am I supposed to do now?

265
00:13:48,994 --> 00:13:50,830
Wait. Like… What's this about?

266
00:13:52,164 --> 00:13:54,416
- There he is!
- Yeah, that's him. Come on.

267
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:57,711
- Yo, seriously?
- Hell yeah. Let's go. Come on.

268
00:13:59,338 --> 00:14:00,464
Hey!

269
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:02,258
- Yo!
- Sup, loser?

270
00:14:06,262 --> 00:14:08,889
Oh, sorry. We didn't realize
you were there.

271
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:11,058
Vroom, vroom.

272
00:14:11,141 --> 00:14:13,602
- Vroom, vroom!
- See you around!

273
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:18,274
Why didn't you say anything?

274
00:14:19,066 --> 00:14:21,235
Doesn't matter. Leave me alone.

275
00:14:26,031 --> 00:14:31,078
And now, using a microscope, let's observe
the flow of blood in the capillaries.

276
00:14:31,161 --> 00:14:35,583
After you've had a chance to observe,
talk with your group about what you see.

277
00:14:36,458 --> 00:14:38,544
- Okay, yes, Miss.
- Go ahead.

278
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:42,298
Look! Look!

279
00:14:43,465 --> 00:14:45,009
Hey, look. Is that her?

280
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:47,845
- The doctor who got cancelled!
- No way!

281
00:14:49,346 --> 00:14:50,931
Whoa, that's crazy.

282
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:53,559
- Let's settle down, please.
- For real?

283
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:57,521
Quiet down, class. That's enough now!

284
00:14:58,022 --> 00:15:00,357
Focus on your group discussions.

285
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:13,746
Takeru.

286
00:15:15,956 --> 00:15:17,082
Where'd he go?

287
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:18,250
- Bathroom.
- Oh yeah?

288
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:20,419
- Excuse me. Are you Takeru's sister?
- Yes.

289
00:15:20,502 --> 00:15:23,881
The PTA board meeting
is going to be starting at about noon.

290
00:15:23,964 --> 00:15:26,592
- The board meeting?
- Yeah. Today.

291
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:28,302
- Thank you so much.
- Excuse me.

292
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:37,311
You want to film the facelift?

293
00:15:37,394 --> 00:15:39,188
Yes. If we can.

294
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:43,859
Mr. Hamaguchi, I just want to make sure
that you understand the situation.

295
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:48,364
It's a complex surgery where we lift skin
from the face under general anesthesia.

296
00:15:48,447 --> 00:15:49,907
Given Mrs. Yuriko's condition, it--

297
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:51,367
No, we understand.

298
00:15:51,867 --> 00:15:55,829
We want to document the procedure
precisely because of the complexity.

299
00:15:57,414 --> 00:15:59,959
Doctor, I've just got a feeling

300
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:02,252
this documentary's gonna go viral.

301
00:16:03,253 --> 00:16:04,964
I promise we won't be in the way.

302
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:08,258
And it's not like we need a big crew.
Do you think you could make it work?

303
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:15,766
Hello, everyone, hello!
Sorry I'm late. Hello.

304
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:19,478
Ms. Osawa, you got another
hyaluronic acid treatment, didn't you?

305
00:16:19,561 --> 00:16:22,398
- You can tell?
- Oh yeah, but who's counting?!

306
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:26,110
- Where? At Dr. Dong-yeon's?
- Exactly.

307
00:16:27,653 --> 00:16:30,030
This is pretty much
what we always talk about.

308
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:33,575
Moms talk about cosmetic surgery now?

309
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:36,328
I never have that much to say myself.

310
00:16:37,621 --> 00:16:40,290
How's your mother?
Is she doing any better? Was it cirrhosis?

311
00:16:40,374 --> 00:16:42,084
Yeah, but she's okay now.

312
00:16:42,584 --> 00:16:43,919
And I made her quit drinking.

313
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:45,796
Please, wish her well for me.

314
00:16:45,879 --> 00:16:47,047
- Thanks.
- My pleasure.

315
00:16:48,632 --> 00:16:50,300
Are you Takeru's sister?

316
00:16:51,385 --> 00:16:53,846
- Yeah.
- It must have been difficult.

317
00:16:53,929 --> 00:16:55,764
All the backlash to deal with.

318
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:57,891
We were all shocked.

319
00:16:57,975 --> 00:16:59,601
And very concerned.

320
00:17:00,352 --> 00:17:01,353
Weren't we?

321
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:05,232
Oh. Well, I'm sorry if I was a burden.

322
00:17:05,315 --> 00:17:06,734
Takeru will be fine.

323
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:10,821
The PTA will take charge
of communicating with the school.

324
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:13,949
He'll have what he needs.
It's all under control.

325
00:17:15,409 --> 00:17:16,243
Right.

326
00:17:30,549 --> 00:17:31,633
Mom?

327
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:33,761
Oh, Mikana. Hey, sweetie.

328
00:17:34,595 --> 00:17:36,638
You came all the way out here
again to shop?

329
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:39,850
The trick is to come after 4 p.m.,
when things get marked down.

330
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:42,061
Come on, that's so embarrassing.

331
00:17:42,978 --> 00:17:44,980
And you wore that outfit
to the last PTA meeting.

332
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,690
What? I didn't. Or did I?

333
00:17:46,774 --> 00:17:50,152
Oh, wow. How could you forget that?

334
00:17:50,903 --> 00:17:54,156
Okay, don't worry. I don't think
anyone cares about my clothes.

335
00:17:56,700 --> 00:18:00,370
Oh, hey, have you talked to Dad yet
about me studying abroad?

336
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:02,956
Uh, maybe he should hear it from you.

337
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:05,542
But he always just says to ask you anyhow.

338
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:07,544
Please, Mom?

339
00:18:08,545 --> 00:18:10,506
Yua and Sana's parents already said yes.

340
00:18:11,006 --> 00:18:12,883
- I'm back.
- Oh, welcome home.

341
00:18:13,425 --> 00:18:16,804
My manager invited me
out for drinks and I'm feeling it.

342
00:18:16,887 --> 00:18:19,056
- I'll just have something light.
- Oh.

343
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:24,228
So Mikana and I were talking…

344
00:18:24,311 --> 00:18:25,395
Yeah?

345
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:28,774
And she wants to study abroad in Hawaii
over summer break.

346
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:31,401
Her best friends are going, apparently.

347
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:32,861
Yeah, sure. Let her do it.

348
00:18:32,945 --> 00:18:35,572
But the exchange rates
are rough right now.

349
00:18:36,073 --> 00:18:37,783
The program's not going to be cheap.

350
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:41,036
Budgeting for the household is your job.
You'll think of something.

351
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:43,497
Sure. I guess.

352
00:18:44,581 --> 00:18:46,959
I was wondering if I should get a job too.

353
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:48,418
Where'd you get that idea?

354
00:18:48,502 --> 00:18:51,880
Well, with two incomes,
we would have more options.

355
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:55,092
Fewer women stay home.
Most of them go back to work eventually.

356
00:18:55,175 --> 00:18:57,302
I don't wanna have
this conversation again.

357
00:18:57,386 --> 00:19:00,472
You agreed to be a stay-at-home mom
until Mikana graduates.

358
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:05,102
Besides, you've been out of the workforce
for ten years. Who would hire you?

359
00:19:05,185 --> 00:19:07,271
I won't have you
working at some supermarket.

360
00:19:07,354 --> 00:19:09,148
It's embarrassing.
Don't even think about it.

361
00:19:11,984 --> 00:19:13,110
I guess you're right.

362
00:19:15,654 --> 00:19:17,447
<i>Welcome back. What will happen?</i>

363
00:19:19,116 --> 00:19:20,534
<i>Are you ready to play?</i>

364
00:19:22,578 --> 00:19:25,747
Mr. Watanabe's blood work
results were due to arrive today.

365
00:19:25,831 --> 00:19:26,957
Do you know if they did?

366
00:19:27,457 --> 00:19:28,667
The fate line.

367
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:31,670
- I'll ask. Be right back.
- Sounds good.

368
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:34,715
Dr. Tanuma's final battle
is about to begin.

369
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:39,553
You hold your patient's future
in your hands.

370
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:45,642
Ms. Yuriko, are you feeling comfortable?

371
00:19:46,351 --> 00:19:48,270
Yes. I'm fine, thanks.

372
00:19:48,353 --> 00:19:49,938
Before we begin,

373
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:53,233
I'd like to ask you
about something important.

374
00:19:53,942 --> 00:19:55,110
Go on.

375
00:19:58,322 --> 00:19:59,573
This, ma'am,

376
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:02,492
is the contract we signed before today.

377
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:04,411
It states that we won't film

378
00:20:04,494 --> 00:20:07,539
any of the procedures
performed under general anesthesia.

379
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:12,169
However, the documentary director
asked if we could make an exception.

380
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:13,712
MEMORANDUM

381
00:20:13,795 --> 00:20:15,964
If it's all right with you, Ms. Yuriko,

382
00:20:16,715 --> 00:20:18,550
we'd like your permission
to film your surgery.

383
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:43,283
THIS IS TRIBEAU, THE COSMETIC BOOKING APP!

384
00:20:45,619 --> 00:20:47,955
BROWSE CLINICS BY BODY PART

385
00:20:54,544 --> 00:20:56,421
- Administering anesthesia--
- Doctor, wait.

386
00:20:56,505 --> 00:21:00,717
Um Is there some way that we can
make the injection painless too?

387
00:21:01,218 --> 00:21:03,053
- How long?
- 20 minutes.

388
00:21:03,136 --> 00:21:05,430
- We've applied the anesthetic.
- Right.

389
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:08,267
All right, here we go.
Beginning the procedure.

390
00:21:09,393 --> 00:21:10,477
Ah, it hurts.

391
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:11,979
You can feel this?

392
00:21:12,062 --> 00:21:13,814
Uh, well, it hurts.

393
00:21:14,314 --> 00:21:15,399
So, you can?

394
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:20,988
YURIKO SAKASHITA

395
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:23,532
Excellent. Thank you so much.

396
00:21:25,867 --> 00:21:27,995
Great. Let's hope
the documentary is a hit.

397
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:31,206
Yes. The next step is the tests, then?

398
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:34,459
Doctor?

399
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:42,134
- Ms. Yuriko.
- Yes?

400
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:47,389
I'd like to recommend that

401
00:21:47,889 --> 00:21:49,308
you reconsider your planned surgery.

402
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:50,475
What?

403
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:56,398
You've made some great progress
so far, Ms. Yuriko,

404
00:21:56,898 --> 00:21:58,483
and you're already so beautiful.

405
00:21:58,567 --> 00:22:01,194
I don't really understand
why you'd want to undergo a facelift.

406
00:22:01,278 --> 00:22:04,364
Doctor, you were the one who said
it would give me the best results.

407
00:22:04,448 --> 00:22:05,615
And that is true.

408
00:22:06,825 --> 00:22:07,951
However,

409
00:22:08,744 --> 00:22:10,662
it's also true
that it will put a lot of stress--

410
00:22:10,746 --> 00:22:12,873
Yes, I'm well aware of the risks, Doctor.

411
00:22:12,956 --> 00:22:14,916
But if this surgery can change me,

412
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:17,586
if it can make me beautiful,
then I want to take the risk.

413
00:22:17,669 --> 00:22:20,964
I'm not like you.
This may be my only opportunity!

414
00:22:33,935 --> 00:22:35,437
I understand.

415
00:22:45,697 --> 00:22:49,368
COSMETIC SURGERY TURNED MY LIFE AROUND

416
00:22:50,827 --> 00:22:54,247
Doctor, it's not like
the surgery's that dangerous, is it?

417
00:22:55,874 --> 00:23:00,712
I mean, as your legal counsel,
I need to be very clear that if

418
00:23:01,463 --> 00:23:04,424
the unthinkable were to happen
during the filming--

419
00:23:04,508 --> 00:23:06,593
She signed the consent form, didn't she?

420
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:10,097
She's already made up her mind, okay?

421
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:13,517
All right then.

422
00:23:14,059 --> 00:23:15,060
Guess I'll be going.

423
00:23:22,984 --> 00:23:24,486
Dearest God…

424
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:27,656
…this man desires better luck.

425
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:29,658
Improve his fortune, God.

426
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:40,794
A doctor praying for help with a patient.

427
00:23:41,586 --> 00:23:42,879
Is that a problem?

428
00:23:43,672 --> 00:23:45,632
I just wonder about the optics of it.

429
00:23:45,715 --> 00:23:47,092
It's more that

430
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:50,595
I don't think my skills
can improve a patient's luck.

431
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:53,723
But don't worry.
I'll stay on the dark side.

432
00:23:53,807 --> 00:23:56,017
I can even study up on spot removal.

433
00:23:57,894 --> 00:23:58,854
Actually,

434
00:23:59,563 --> 00:24:00,689
why are you here?

435
00:24:01,898 --> 00:24:03,775
You're not praying
for help with a patient?

436
00:24:06,653 --> 00:24:08,905
- That's not a problem, I hope?
- Nah.

437
00:24:09,906 --> 00:24:10,907
Ironic.

438
00:24:11,408 --> 00:24:13,660
That The Hand of God
would be praying to God.

439
00:24:13,743 --> 00:24:15,162
Have a good day.

440
00:24:29,342 --> 00:24:33,138
I have a feeling we're going
to work up a sweat. It's so warm today.

441
00:24:36,475 --> 00:24:39,060
- Oh! I'm sorry, dear.
- Is everything all right?

442
00:24:39,144 --> 00:24:42,731
Why don't we sit down?
Here, take your time. Rest.

443
00:24:43,231 --> 00:24:44,065
There.

444
00:24:47,110 --> 00:24:49,571
I'm going to take
Ms. Yuriko home now, Doctor.

445
00:24:50,071 --> 00:24:51,364
Would you mind coming with me?

446
00:24:52,324 --> 00:24:53,366
Go with you?

447
00:24:54,201 --> 00:24:55,744
Having a doctor would be better.

448
00:24:56,244 --> 00:24:58,914
Both the director and Dr. Rui
have appointments, you see.

449
00:25:00,957 --> 00:25:02,334
Just give me a minute.

450
00:25:04,753 --> 00:25:07,130
- Let's take it easy.
- Of course. Thank you, dear.

451
00:25:09,174 --> 00:25:11,968
- I'll take your blood pressure.
- Sorry for the trouble.

452
00:25:12,469 --> 00:25:16,598
I barely went out and I'm already dizzy.
Can you believe it?

453
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:20,185
- Ms. Yuriko?
- Yes?

454
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:21,728
Does the filming bother you?

455
00:25:21,811 --> 00:25:25,899
No, not at all. It's funny,
it makes me feel like I'm dreaming.

456
00:25:27,150 --> 00:25:30,362
My husband would be so shocked
if he could see me now.

457
00:25:31,154 --> 00:25:33,073
Blood pressure's a little low.

458
00:25:33,156 --> 00:25:33,990
Right.

459
00:25:34,908 --> 00:25:36,243
- Ms. Yuriko?
- Yes?

460
00:25:36,743 --> 00:25:38,453
I'd like you to rest for a few days.

461
00:25:38,537 --> 00:25:39,663
Yes.

462
00:25:47,212 --> 00:25:49,464
Is everything all right?

463
00:25:56,930 --> 00:25:59,182
- Labored breathing.
- I'll go get a towel.

464
00:25:59,683 --> 00:26:00,850
Ms. Yuriko,

465
00:26:01,351 --> 00:26:02,811
I'd like to listen to your lungs.

466
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:08,316
It'll be over soon. I'm completely fine.

467
00:26:09,901 --> 00:26:11,820
- Ms. Yuriko.
- Hm?

468
00:26:11,903 --> 00:26:15,282
It would seem that the cancer
may have spread to your lungs.

469
00:26:15,907 --> 00:26:17,242
I'd like to call an ambulance.

470
00:26:17,325 --> 00:26:19,160
No, no, it'll stop soon.

471
00:26:19,244 --> 00:26:20,996
I have to, for your own good

472
00:26:21,496 --> 00:26:22,956
Don't do it!

473
00:26:24,082 --> 00:26:26,293
Please don't. I hate hospitals.

474
00:26:30,922 --> 00:26:32,674
Here. You can rinse your mouth.

475
00:26:36,803 --> 00:26:39,347
No. I'm sorry. I can't do this anymore.

476
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:43,727
I don't think you understand.
Your life is in danger, facelift or no.

477
00:26:43,810 --> 00:26:46,563
If you keep pushing with no regard
for the consequences, it's pointless.

478
00:26:46,646 --> 00:26:50,025
You don't understand, Doctor.
It doesn't matter if I die.

479
00:26:50,108 --> 00:26:52,944
I just want them to leave me alone!

480
00:26:57,032 --> 00:26:59,618
They told me the same thing
at the hospital.

481
00:27:00,994 --> 00:27:02,662
But doctors don't…

482
00:27:02,746 --> 00:27:05,832
They don't care about
how their patients feel. Not really.

483
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:08,084
They just pity us and look down on us.

484
00:27:09,336 --> 00:27:11,504
- They don't. That's not true.
- They do!

485
00:27:11,588 --> 00:27:13,256
They all do, and so do you.

486
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:15,258
You think I'm stupid, don't you, Doctor?

487
00:27:18,637 --> 00:27:22,015
Despite what my body's going through,
I still want to be beautiful.

488
00:27:22,515 --> 00:27:25,435
And you pity me!
You think I'm pathetic, don't you?

489
00:27:30,398 --> 00:27:32,150
You should rest. Lie back.

490
00:27:37,739 --> 00:27:38,948
I'm nearing the end.

491
00:27:40,075 --> 00:27:41,785
I know. I know I am.

492
00:27:42,869 --> 00:27:44,788
And at the end, I just…

493
00:27:45,288 --> 00:27:49,793
I wanted to do something
that was just for me and no one else.

494
00:27:50,335 --> 00:27:53,713
That's all I really want now.

495
00:27:57,092 --> 00:28:01,012
Even if the thing I want is silly or vain.

496
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:05,141
Over the course of my life, I've learned

497
00:28:05,725 --> 00:28:07,477
everyone has needs.

498
00:28:09,813 --> 00:28:10,897
All of us.

499
00:28:10,980 --> 00:28:12,857
Important or frivolous.

500
00:28:13,525 --> 00:28:17,195
We all need something
that means the world to us.

501
00:28:33,837 --> 00:28:36,339
I never deliberately looked down on her.

502
00:28:36,423 --> 00:28:38,383
I never pitied her. I swear.

503
00:28:42,178 --> 00:28:44,097
Is that how it was with Kana?

504
00:28:44,806 --> 00:28:46,891
- Sorry?
- Kanabun.

505
00:28:48,518 --> 00:28:51,688
You thought it was ridiculous
to get implants when she had a tumor.

506
00:28:52,981 --> 00:28:54,190
That's not looking down on her?

507
00:28:57,068 --> 00:28:59,279
I happen to agree with Ms. Yuriko,

508
00:28:59,362 --> 00:29:01,614
as hard as it may be to accept.

509
00:29:02,699 --> 00:29:04,993
As much as you may not want
to admit it, Doctor.

510
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:19,716
I'm home.

511
00:29:19,799 --> 00:29:21,926
Hi, honey. Do you mind having dinner now?

512
00:29:23,011 --> 00:29:24,554
Uh, because Daddy's late.

513
00:29:26,014 --> 00:29:27,223
He's still working?

514
00:29:27,307 --> 00:29:28,600
He just texted, yeah.

515
00:29:28,683 --> 00:29:30,894
I bet it's another drinking party.

516
00:29:32,687 --> 00:29:36,858
Oh, right, so about you studying overseas,

517
00:29:37,567 --> 00:29:39,360
well, Poppa said yeah!

518
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:41,196
He did? For real?

519
00:29:41,696 --> 00:29:45,700
On one condition. You have to come back
even smarter than you are now. Okay?

520
00:29:47,410 --> 00:29:49,996
- Mm-hmm.
- Now let's eat!

521
00:29:55,543 --> 00:29:56,836
<i>I'll kill myself!</i>

522
00:29:56,920 --> 00:29:58,963
Let me be clear.
I had to take the silicone out

523
00:29:59,047 --> 00:30:01,174
because you were in critical condition
and about to die.

524
00:30:01,257 --> 00:30:05,011
If I hadn't taken it out, you might
have died! What don't you get, you moron?

525
00:30:05,094 --> 00:30:06,012
I wanna die!

526
00:30:08,097 --> 00:30:11,601
Despite what my body's going through,
I still want to be beautiful.

527
00:30:12,101 --> 00:30:14,687
And you pity me!
You think I'm pathetic, don't you?

528
00:30:50,682 --> 00:30:51,933
Unknown number.

529
00:30:54,894 --> 00:30:56,813
- Hello?
- Hi.

530
00:30:57,605 --> 00:30:58,565
It's Numata.

531
00:30:59,524 --> 00:31:00,400
Yes?

532
00:31:02,527 --> 00:31:04,612
I need to ask you for a favor.

533
00:31:05,321 --> 00:31:07,699
Hi! How are you? Just these.

534
00:31:08,199 --> 00:31:11,870
- You've got a lot today.
- Yeah, we've got a lot of stuff today.

535
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:13,580
Let me take a look.

536
00:31:14,372 --> 00:31:16,332
UPDATE ON DRY CLEANING PRICES

537
00:31:17,584 --> 00:31:20,461
Uh, sorry. It'll just be the suit, please.

538
00:31:20,545 --> 00:31:22,380
I forgot something at home.

539
00:32:06,007 --> 00:32:07,050
I, um…

540
00:32:09,552 --> 00:32:10,386
I need to tell you--

541
00:32:10,470 --> 00:32:12,347
You're the doctor from the university.

542
00:32:13,723 --> 00:32:15,308
I've seen your picture online.

543
00:32:17,936 --> 00:32:18,770
Yes.

544
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:28,363
I didn't know Ms. Kana well…

545
00:32:31,407 --> 00:32:34,077
but for her, there was something
more valuable than life.

546
00:32:36,037 --> 00:32:37,246
I couldn't understand that.

547
00:32:41,459 --> 00:32:43,836
There's nothing I can do
that will bring her back.

548
00:32:48,007 --> 00:32:49,008
I'm sorry.

549
00:32:52,387 --> 00:32:53,972
I'm truly sorry, ma'am.

550
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:21,416
I would have done the same thing
if I were you.

551
00:33:23,835 --> 00:33:24,669
What?

552
00:33:25,253 --> 00:33:28,381
She had a tumor,
but still wanted her implants.

553
00:33:28,881 --> 00:33:30,967
It's crazy. It's unreasonable.

554
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:35,304
Any doctor would think that.

555
00:33:40,727 --> 00:33:42,145
But here's the thing.

556
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:46,065
That was the only way
she knew how to live.

557
00:33:49,444 --> 00:33:51,612
Up until junior high, she was a shut-in.

558
00:33:55,158 --> 00:33:58,244
But when she started getting surgery,
her life was transformed.

559
00:33:59,454 --> 00:34:01,914
She got scouted by a modeling agency.

560
00:34:02,415 --> 00:34:04,584
People knew her. They loved her.

561
00:34:05,168 --> 00:34:08,755
She shined so bright
that she became a star.

562
00:34:12,425 --> 00:34:13,968
Deep down, though,

563
00:34:16,471 --> 00:34:18,347
she was in terrible agony.

564
00:34:21,309 --> 00:34:24,562
She was suffering
because none of it was real.

565
00:34:27,273 --> 00:34:29,150
None of it. It was all a lie.

566
00:34:30,443 --> 00:34:33,780
Her date of birth, her hometown,
her graduation photo,

567
00:34:33,863 --> 00:34:35,364
her Wikipedia page.

568
00:34:35,448 --> 00:34:37,575
Even the name, Kana Kokubun.

569
00:34:39,077 --> 00:34:40,161
It was all made-up.

570
00:34:40,244 --> 00:34:42,955
It was crafted, just like her appearance.

571
00:34:55,468 --> 00:34:56,511
She…

572
00:34:57,386 --> 00:35:00,181
She was so desperate to hide her pain.

573
00:35:00,681 --> 00:35:02,934
But she could never outrun it.

574
00:35:04,685 --> 00:35:08,314
I always knew
it would end up catching her one day.

575
00:35:35,383 --> 00:35:37,009
This was my daughter.

576
00:35:38,427 --> 00:35:40,930
She was more real than Kanabun.

577
00:35:41,722 --> 00:35:43,724
Her name was Akari Shimoda.

578
00:36:10,459 --> 00:36:14,255
I looked into the rumors about the
chairman renting a property for a clinic.

579
00:36:14,839 --> 00:36:17,175
From what I could tell,
it seems to be true.

580
00:36:17,675 --> 00:36:20,678
He's aiming to have it in operation
by the end of the year.

581
00:36:21,220 --> 00:36:22,305
And so,

582
00:36:23,514 --> 00:36:28,394
would you like me to try to find out more
about the chairman's plans for the clinic?

583
00:36:31,564 --> 00:36:32,523
Ma'am?

584
00:36:37,069 --> 00:36:38,196
There's no need.

585
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:43,576
I'll just ask him myself
the next time I see him. Thank you.

586
00:36:58,841 --> 00:37:01,886
SUCCESSOR OF THE HAND OF GOD

587
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:06,933
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

588
00:37:09,894 --> 00:37:11,771
- Today's the day.
- Yes.

589
00:37:12,271 --> 00:37:14,023
Time for the facelift.

590
00:37:17,401 --> 00:37:20,613
- Beautiful day for it.
- Yes, it's gorgeous, isn't it?

591
00:37:35,336 --> 00:37:39,215
<i>There's talk that the Tohyama</i>
<i>director made a critical medical error,</i>

592
00:37:39,298 --> 00:37:42,635
<i>and that a lot of clients</i>
<i>are leaving for other clinics.</i>

593
00:37:53,521 --> 00:37:54,522
What is it, Rin?

594
00:37:58,442 --> 00:38:02,363
<i>The fact is that Dr. Arata</i>
<i>made his name as "The Hand of God."</i>

595
00:38:02,446 --> 00:38:03,864
<i>But that's Dr. Arata.</i>

596
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:06,117
<i>Why would I believe you're as good as him?</i>

597
00:38:06,200 --> 00:38:08,077
<i>I think you're pushing it.</i>

598
00:38:10,246 --> 00:38:13,082
Ah, this is great. Wow.

599
00:38:13,666 --> 00:38:15,918
Is this doctor supposed to be me?

600
00:38:16,002 --> 00:38:18,546
So then, this one must be you, Rin.

601
00:38:18,629 --> 00:38:20,339
I see.

602
00:38:20,965 --> 00:38:24,885
Well, then, you must want to be a doctor,
just like Daddy.

603
00:38:33,978 --> 00:38:36,355
<i>You must want to be a doctor,</i>
<i>just like Daddy.</i>

604
00:38:39,608 --> 00:38:40,985
<i>Now we can't film?</i>

605
00:38:41,610 --> 00:38:43,988
Come on, Doctor.
I was just with her. She was excited.

606
00:38:44,071 --> 00:38:46,532
The decision has nothing
to do with Mrs. Yuriko.

607
00:38:46,615 --> 00:38:48,451
It was a clinic-wide amendment.

608
00:38:48,534 --> 00:38:51,704
I understand, Doctor,
but it's just so sudden.

609
00:38:54,957 --> 00:38:57,126
Raise the right side by 0.5 millimeters.

610
00:38:57,209 --> 00:38:58,336
Dr. Rui.

611
00:38:58,919 --> 00:39:01,130
Would you mind giving us a minute, please?

612
00:39:01,213 --> 00:39:02,798
Mm. Sure.

613
00:39:06,719 --> 00:39:09,221
Yes? What is it?

614
00:39:12,308 --> 00:39:15,227
I wanted to speak to you
about Mrs. Yuriko's facelift.

615
00:39:18,230 --> 00:39:21,067
I want you to perform her surgery.

616
00:39:22,818 --> 00:39:23,652
What?

617
00:39:24,695 --> 00:39:25,780
Impossible.

618
00:39:27,531 --> 00:39:28,574
I don't get it. Why?

619
00:39:28,657 --> 00:39:31,577
We don't have time
to get into the details. I'm sorry.

620
00:39:31,660 --> 00:39:33,913
But rest assured,
I'll be there to support you.

621
00:39:33,996 --> 00:39:37,416
No! I refuse to do it.
And you knew I would refuse.

622
00:39:37,917 --> 00:39:40,878
I was against her getting the surgery
to begin with. You know that!

623
00:39:40,961 --> 00:39:43,047
I can't be the only option to perform it.

624
00:39:43,631 --> 00:39:46,967
Unless you decided it was too dangerous.
It'd explain why you're making me do it.

625
00:39:47,051 --> 00:39:48,928
- It's not like that.
- Then why me?

626
00:39:49,011 --> 00:39:51,055
It can't be me. It has to be you!

627
00:40:05,569 --> 00:40:07,321
If anything does go wrong,

628
00:40:08,406 --> 00:40:10,199
I'll assume all responsibility.

629
00:40:14,245 --> 00:40:18,958
My dress shirts have to be
dry cleaned. I told you, didn't I?

630
00:40:19,041 --> 00:40:22,169
It's just that the
dry cleaner's is so expensive. I thought--

631
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:24,922
You thought what? You can't be serious.

632
00:40:27,216 --> 00:40:29,385
What could it cost? A hundred yen? Two?

633
00:40:29,468 --> 00:40:33,806
I guess. I… I know it doesn't seem
like much, but it can really add up.

634
00:40:33,889 --> 00:40:37,184
You know
what your problem is? You're cheap.

635
00:40:38,352 --> 00:40:41,147
I'm not asking for much. Am I?

636
00:40:41,230 --> 00:40:44,608
All I'm asking for is for you
to do something simple. Isn't that right?

637
00:40:44,692 --> 00:40:46,026
Mm-hmm. I'm sorry, you're right.

638
00:40:46,110 --> 00:40:47,111
- I know.
- No problem.

639
00:40:47,903 --> 00:40:49,196
I'll take them now, then.

640
00:40:50,865 --> 00:40:52,533
I'm such a scatterbrain.

641
00:41:00,207 --> 00:41:02,334
Last-minute cancellations suck.

642
00:41:02,835 --> 00:41:03,794
Oh yeah.

643
00:41:09,008 --> 00:41:10,968
- Oh! Here she comes.
- Hey, roll camera!

644
00:41:11,051 --> 00:41:11,886
Rolling.

645
00:41:12,970 --> 00:41:14,972
Here comes The Hand of God. Get a shot.

646
00:41:19,226 --> 00:41:22,271
All right, Ms. Yuriko.
If you're ready, we'll begin.

647
00:41:22,354 --> 00:41:24,732
I'm ready. I'm in your hands, Doctor.

648
00:41:25,566 --> 00:41:27,693
As soon as she's out of surgery,
we'll be ready, okay?

649
00:41:27,776 --> 00:41:28,986
Yes, of course.

650
00:41:30,112 --> 00:41:31,197
This way.

651
00:41:35,743 --> 00:41:36,994
Just in here.

652
00:41:42,917 --> 00:41:44,585
Administering anesthetic.

653
00:41:44,668 --> 00:41:45,503
Good.

654
00:41:55,846 --> 00:41:58,390
Doctor, we're ready for you now.

655
00:42:16,367 --> 00:42:18,035
Beginning with the skin incision.

656
00:42:18,536 --> 00:42:20,037
- Scalpel.
- Scalpel.

657
00:42:49,233 --> 00:42:50,943
- Swap out the gauze.
- Okay.

658
00:43:13,382 --> 00:43:15,217
Director, look at her blood pressure.

659
00:43:18,220 --> 00:43:19,221
It's all right.

660
00:43:20,222 --> 00:43:21,223
You can continue.

661
00:43:49,835 --> 00:43:51,712
I'm not gonna study abroad.

662
00:43:52,212 --> 00:43:54,298
Wait, what? Where's this coming from?

663
00:43:54,798 --> 00:43:56,550
I've been saving up for you to go.

664
00:43:57,051 --> 00:43:59,720
Your father and I
have both made sacrifices for this.

665
00:43:59,803 --> 00:44:02,139
You mean you've made sacrifices.

666
00:44:02,222 --> 00:44:05,309
Come on. That's not fair,
and it's not even true.

667
00:44:06,143 --> 00:44:08,020
Mom, you're not happy, are you?

668
00:44:12,691 --> 00:44:16,445
You never get new clothes for yourself.
You buy groceries really far away.

669
00:44:16,528 --> 00:44:18,697
I do that because I want to.
I like the exercise--

670
00:44:18,781 --> 00:44:20,282
No. I don't believe you!

671
00:44:20,366 --> 00:44:21,575
Honey…

672
00:44:22,451 --> 00:44:23,744
That store's the best.

673
00:44:24,244 --> 00:44:27,247
They have great cuts of meat,
the produce is always fresh--

674
00:44:27,331 --> 00:44:29,667
- No, stop lying to me!
- I'm not lying to you!

675
00:44:30,834 --> 00:44:33,629
Mommy's happy living here
with you and your father.

676
00:44:33,712 --> 00:44:35,381
I'm not giving anything up.

677
00:44:55,901 --> 00:44:57,403
I don't think she can handle any more.

678
00:44:59,697 --> 00:45:02,074
- Director, this is--
- I'll help with the sutures.

679
00:45:03,450 --> 00:45:05,953
- Let's hurry.
- Ms. Takahashi, raise the bed.

680
00:45:08,163 --> 00:45:09,540
- Turning her head.
- Careful.

681
00:45:09,623 --> 00:45:10,833
There we go.

682
00:45:18,173 --> 00:45:19,758
Wipe the incision, please.

683
00:45:29,643 --> 00:45:30,853
Thank you.

684
00:45:50,581 --> 00:45:52,166
Mom, you're not happy, are you?

685
00:45:57,296 --> 00:45:58,130
Sorry!

686
00:45:59,548 --> 00:46:01,049
- It's okay.
- Are you hurt?

687
00:46:01,133 --> 00:46:03,427
No, I'm fine. I'm fine. Sorry. Thanks.

688
00:46:03,927 --> 00:46:04,845
Sorry.

689
00:46:39,379 --> 00:46:41,465
Is it finished? How is Ms. Yuriko?

690
00:46:44,426 --> 00:46:45,552
She's doing well.

691
00:46:46,220 --> 00:46:47,554
The surgery was a success.

692
00:46:52,351 --> 00:46:53,602
Five hours.

693
00:46:54,645 --> 00:46:55,646
That was long.

694
00:46:55,729 --> 00:46:58,732
I had no idea that the surgery
would be this complicated.

695
00:47:00,400 --> 00:47:01,401
I'm sorry.

696
00:47:02,402 --> 00:47:03,737
You can film now.

697
00:47:04,446 --> 00:47:05,906
- Right, let's go.
- Okay.

698
00:47:08,408 --> 00:47:09,326
Excuse us.

699
00:47:15,541 --> 00:47:17,167
Excuse us. We'll stay out of your way.

700
00:47:17,251 --> 00:47:19,461
- Excuse us.
- Shoot from that side.

701
00:47:19,545 --> 00:47:20,546
You got it.

702
00:47:21,839 --> 00:47:24,091
- Wow.
- Hi. Sorry.

703
00:47:42,025 --> 00:47:43,652
Kana's mom called.

704
00:47:46,780 --> 00:47:50,492
She said that you two had a talk
and that you apologized.

705
00:47:53,453 --> 00:47:54,621
Thank you for that.

706
00:47:55,664 --> 00:47:58,083
Oh. No, I'm the one that should thank you.

707
00:47:59,209 --> 00:48:00,168
Really. Thanks.

708
00:48:02,713 --> 00:48:04,506
Who's staying here tonight? You?

709
00:48:05,048 --> 00:48:07,342
I'm not, no. It's the director.

710
00:48:08,093 --> 00:48:09,177
The director?

711
00:48:09,678 --> 00:48:13,015
She's been sleeping here ever
since Ms. Yuriko's surgery was booked.

712
00:48:13,098 --> 00:48:14,683
Wanted to stay close.

713
00:48:15,225 --> 00:48:17,352
She worries, even if she doesn't show it.

714
00:48:19,187 --> 00:48:22,149
If she says she wants to die, you'll just
kill her? You lost your damn mind?

715
00:48:22,232 --> 00:48:24,067
Someone who doesn't have much time left

716
00:48:24,151 --> 00:48:26,737
is asking for one last chance
to be beautiful!

717
00:48:26,820 --> 00:48:29,573
I'm a doctor. How can I deny her that?

718
00:48:30,699 --> 00:48:32,910
Life isn't just quantity.
It's also quality.

719
00:48:33,994 --> 00:48:36,496
<i>There are ways to help</i>
<i>besides chemotherapy.</i>

720
00:48:42,252 --> 00:48:44,588
Huh. She's known for a while.

721
00:48:46,214 --> 00:48:49,134
The counseling session.
That's when she realized it.

722
00:48:49,968 --> 00:48:50,844
What?

723
00:48:53,597 --> 00:48:54,640
That Ms. Yuriko

724
00:48:55,849 --> 00:48:58,477
wouldn't be satisfied
with only a longer life.

725
00:49:04,524 --> 00:49:05,901
Honestly, I, um…

726
00:49:08,236 --> 00:49:10,530
I never thought about it like that before.

727
00:49:20,374 --> 00:49:21,792
<i>I looked into the rumors</i>

728
00:49:21,875 --> 00:49:24,836
<i>about the chairman</i>
<i>renting a property for a clinic.</i>

729
00:49:24,920 --> 00:49:26,546
<i>It seems to be true.</i>

730
00:49:34,471 --> 00:49:37,265
Mikana, can I come in? I wanna talk.

731
00:49:39,017 --> 00:49:40,811
I'm not hungry.

732
00:49:41,812 --> 00:49:45,232
No, it's not that, honey.
It's about studying overseas.

733
00:49:55,200 --> 00:49:58,912
Go on, take it. If it makes you happy,
then you should do it.

734
00:50:00,205 --> 00:50:03,417
You know what? I've decided
I want to do what makes me happy too.

735
00:50:09,506 --> 00:50:12,092
I have some money
I've been saving up in secret.

736
00:50:25,605 --> 00:50:26,815
A walk-in?

737
00:50:26,898 --> 00:50:29,943
That's right. She wanted
to have the work done today.

738
00:50:30,027 --> 00:50:32,612
And I thought I'd at least ask
since one of your operations

739
00:50:32,696 --> 00:50:33,905
was cancelled this afternoon.

740
00:50:33,989 --> 00:50:36,158
- Pencil her in.
- Of course, Doctor.

741
00:50:36,241 --> 00:50:37,826
What surgery is it she's asking about?

742
00:50:40,412 --> 00:50:41,955
Don't be nervous.

743
00:50:42,456 --> 00:50:44,666
The doctors here are wonderful. Very kind.

744
00:50:49,755 --> 00:50:51,423
- Come in.
- Ma'am?

745
00:50:51,506 --> 00:50:52,799
Go on in.

746
00:50:53,383 --> 00:50:55,844
You can put your personal items
on the couch.

747
00:51:00,057 --> 00:51:02,934
Excuse me. The woman
who just came in, what's she here for?

748
00:51:03,018 --> 00:51:04,686
Oh, female genital surgery.

749
00:51:05,520 --> 00:51:06,730
What procedure?

750
00:51:06,813 --> 00:51:08,440
A labia minora reduction.

751
00:51:08,940 --> 00:51:09,983
It's funny, though.

752
00:51:10,067 --> 00:51:13,445
Doing that before her face
is like jumping straight to third base.

753
00:51:13,528 --> 00:51:15,989
Maybe her husband lost interest
after she gave birth.

754
00:51:16,073 --> 00:51:17,616
Yikes! That does happen.

755
00:51:17,699 --> 00:51:19,743
- It's hard, though.
- It is, for sure.

756
00:51:19,826 --> 00:51:22,746
Some patients choose to change
their appearance for themselves.

757
00:51:23,789 --> 00:51:25,373
And she is one of them.

758
00:51:25,874 --> 00:51:28,126
Her husband has nothing to do with it.

759
00:51:29,044 --> 00:51:31,880
She told me she wanted to feel
more confident in her body.

760
00:51:33,173 --> 00:51:36,384
Whether or not they can be seen,
insecurities plague all of us.

761
00:51:37,010 --> 00:51:38,678
It's our job to support people.

762
00:51:38,762 --> 00:51:41,640
- I'm sorry, Doctor.
- Sorry, Doctor.

763
00:51:48,730 --> 00:51:51,525
- Let me know if it hurts, okay?
- I will. Thank you.

764
00:51:57,989 --> 00:51:59,866
All right, we're starting. This may sting.

765
00:51:59,950 --> 00:52:00,784
Okay.

766
00:52:08,250 --> 00:52:10,252
That's done.
Now we'll start the procedure.

767
00:52:10,961 --> 00:52:14,506
If you feel any discomfort, we can
up the anesthetic. Just let us know.

768
00:52:14,589 --> 00:52:15,423
Yes.

769
00:52:26,768 --> 00:52:28,937
Hi, Mrs. Ozawa. We're all done.

770
00:52:30,230 --> 00:52:31,064
What?

771
00:52:33,483 --> 00:52:34,401
You're…

772
00:52:35,527 --> 00:52:36,444
It's over?

773
00:52:36,528 --> 00:52:38,238
Yes, it's all over now.

774
00:52:47,789 --> 00:52:49,624
Is that all right?

775
00:52:49,708 --> 00:52:52,627
I bet you thought
it was going to be a much bigger surgery.

776
00:52:58,341 --> 00:52:59,593
No, it's just that…

777
00:53:01,386 --> 00:53:04,181
I was just wondering why it took so long

778
00:53:04,681 --> 00:53:06,391
for me to do something so simple.

779
00:53:08,226 --> 00:53:11,605
And the more I think about it,
the more I feel silly.

780
00:53:19,738 --> 00:53:21,740
- I'm sorry.
- No.

781
00:53:23,992 --> 00:53:24,826
I'm sorry.

782
00:53:26,745 --> 00:53:28,246
You did so great.

783
00:53:28,330 --> 00:53:31,333
<i>Even if the thing I want is silly or vain.</i>

784
00:53:31,833 --> 00:53:34,502
<i>Over the course of my life, I've learned</i>

785
00:53:35,462 --> 00:53:37,130
everyone has needs.

786
00:53:38,673 --> 00:53:39,758
<i>All of us.</i>

787
00:53:41,927 --> 00:53:45,430
<i>We all need something</i>
<i>that means the world to us.</i>

788
00:54:00,946 --> 00:54:03,114
Doctor, here's your mark. Stand here.

789
00:54:03,615 --> 00:54:05,659
Thank you. Perfect. We're ready?

790
00:54:05,742 --> 00:54:07,619
- Ready, sir.
- Let's roll it.

791
00:54:07,702 --> 00:54:09,788
- Okay, sound speed.
- Speeding.

792
00:54:09,871 --> 00:54:11,831
- Camera.
- Rolling.

793
00:54:11,915 --> 00:54:12,916
We're rolling.

794
00:54:12,999 --> 00:54:14,209
And we're on!

795
00:54:14,751 --> 00:54:17,837
Bring her in three, two…

796
00:54:19,089 --> 00:54:20,090
Cue.

797
00:54:58,920 --> 00:55:02,299
Ms. Yuriko, congratulations.
Please, take these.

798
00:55:02,382 --> 00:55:03,758
Thank you so much.

799
00:55:04,259 --> 00:55:06,594
You look so incredibly beautiful.

800
00:55:07,595 --> 00:55:10,140
Here, this way.

801
00:55:16,730 --> 00:55:17,939
What do you think?

802
00:55:24,195 --> 00:55:27,282
I think I can now die happy.

803
00:55:29,200 --> 00:55:32,245
Oh, enough of that, Ms. Yuriko.

804
00:55:32,329 --> 00:55:34,581
Enjoy your beauty and your new life.

805
00:55:35,081 --> 00:55:40,754
I hate to say it, but a GP would never
be able to do what she did, would they?

806
00:56:17,540 --> 00:56:19,250
- What are you…
- The chairman?

807
00:56:20,168 --> 00:56:21,836
What are you doing here?

808
00:56:21,920 --> 00:56:24,422
I got a call from a pushy TV director.

809
00:56:25,048 --> 00:56:28,259
He asked me if I would check
the final result of the surgery.

810
00:56:33,056 --> 00:56:34,474
My name is Tohyama.

811
00:56:35,809 --> 00:56:38,019
Do you mind if I have a look at you?

812
00:56:38,103 --> 00:56:39,270
Please.

813
00:57:23,314 --> 00:57:24,149
I'm surprised.

814
00:57:26,985 --> 00:57:28,111
She's perfect.

815
00:57:33,116 --> 00:57:36,870
Oh, jeez…
You had me on edge there for a minute.

816
00:57:40,290 --> 00:57:41,541
Congratulations, ma'am.

817
00:57:42,041 --> 00:57:43,751
You're absolutely stunning.

818
00:57:48,173 --> 00:57:49,257
Thank you so much.

819
00:58:00,977 --> 00:58:02,312
Hi, ma'am, welcome.

820
00:58:03,980 --> 00:58:06,483
- Those look great.
- Would you like some? Here you go, then.

821
00:58:06,566 --> 00:58:07,692
- Thanks. Bye.
- Thank you.

822
00:58:08,276 --> 00:58:09,402
Hello. How--

823
00:58:10,862 --> 00:58:12,614
Uh, Mikana…

824
00:58:13,656 --> 00:58:14,699
Mom, what…

825
00:58:20,371 --> 00:58:21,289
Caught red-handed!

826
00:58:23,124 --> 00:58:26,586
Mm. I was
just putting out some fresh fruit.

827
00:58:26,669 --> 00:58:32,050
PHOTO STUDIO MATSUO

828
00:58:33,343 --> 00:58:34,636
Oh! Hello there.

829
00:58:34,719 --> 00:58:35,762
Hello.

830
00:58:38,056 --> 00:58:39,057
Do I…

831
00:58:40,225 --> 00:58:41,434
Ah!

832
00:58:41,518 --> 00:58:45,063
I'm sorry, I didn't recognize you.
You look so different.

833
00:58:45,146 --> 00:58:47,815
I believe the last time you came
was for your husband.

834
00:58:47,899 --> 00:58:50,026
Yes. It was for his memorial.

835
00:58:50,109 --> 00:58:52,070
- Ah, yes, that's right.
- Yeah.

836
00:58:52,153 --> 00:58:54,572
Are you here to celebrate something, then?

837
00:58:55,490 --> 00:58:59,827
I was going to ask you
to take my memorial photo.

838
00:58:59,911 --> 00:59:02,789
Sorry, I don't understand.
Your memorial photo?

839
00:59:02,872 --> 00:59:04,958
Yes.

840
00:59:05,041 --> 00:59:07,001
<i>So, what did you end up getting?</i>

841
00:59:07,085 --> 00:59:10,088
- Hm?
- You used your secret savings.

842
00:59:10,755 --> 00:59:11,756
Can't tell you.

843
00:59:11,839 --> 00:59:13,883
Why not? That's not fair! I wanna know.

844
00:59:13,967 --> 00:59:16,302
I can't tell you now.

845
00:59:16,386 --> 00:59:19,681
But I can tell you
when you graduate from college.

846
00:59:19,764 --> 00:59:22,559
College? Mom, that's, like, so far away.

847
00:59:22,642 --> 00:59:24,727
You'd be surprised how fast it'll go.

848
00:59:25,937 --> 00:59:29,232
Well, your dad will be home late tonight.
Wanna go get something to eat?

849
00:59:29,315 --> 00:59:32,110
Really? Amazing! Yay! Where are we going?

850
00:59:32,193 --> 00:59:33,653
I think you might already know.

851
00:59:34,404 --> 00:59:36,489
Ah… Back to Saize?

852
00:59:36,573 --> 00:59:39,075
I love Saize's, don't you?

853
00:59:39,158 --> 00:59:40,285
Yeah, I do too.

854
00:59:40,368 --> 00:59:43,788
Okay, is there something you'd
rather eat? Tell me. We'll go anywhere.

855
00:59:43,871 --> 00:59:45,707
Hm… What do I want?

856
00:59:48,293 --> 00:59:49,419
Are you ready?

857
01:00:07,312 --> 01:00:09,147
<i>I can't lie, Rin. I'm impressed.</i>

858
01:00:10,231 --> 01:00:12,567
Who would have dared
to do such an intensive procedure

859
01:00:12,650 --> 01:00:14,736
on a terminal cancer patient?

860
01:00:15,486 --> 01:00:16,487
If it airs,

861
01:00:17,530 --> 01:00:19,949
it may well bring a lot of new clients.

862
01:00:20,450 --> 01:00:23,411
When I first heard those rumors,
I was worried, I can't lie.

863
01:00:23,494 --> 01:00:25,246
But you've put my mind at ease.

864
01:00:28,082 --> 01:00:30,126
And speaking of rumors,

865
01:00:30,627 --> 01:00:34,088
there's something I've been meaning
to ask you about as well, actually.

866
01:00:34,172 --> 01:00:35,381
Before that, let me say…

867
01:00:36,424 --> 01:00:39,844
I wouldn't be much of a father
if all I ever did was praise you

868
01:00:39,927 --> 01:00:41,971
without offering feedback.

869
01:00:45,350 --> 01:00:48,353
To be honest with you, her nose…

870
01:00:48,436 --> 01:00:51,564
I wasn't that impressed.
You can do better.

871
01:00:51,648 --> 01:00:54,025
The final shape was ordinary at best.

872
01:00:54,108 --> 01:00:57,487
Hm. Certainly not worthy of our clinic.

873
01:01:00,031 --> 01:01:02,659
Oh. Now, don't make that face.

874
01:01:04,202 --> 01:01:06,162
It wasn't all bad. Right?

875
01:01:06,245 --> 01:01:07,664
The facelift was perfect.

876
01:01:08,164 --> 01:01:09,374
I mean it.

877
01:01:09,999 --> 01:01:12,835
It was truly
the work of my successor, Rin.

878
01:01:23,638 --> 01:01:25,348
I'm so happy to hear that.

879
01:01:25,431 --> 01:01:26,516
Thanks, Dad.

880
01:01:28,935 --> 01:01:30,937
Excuse me. I'll be right back.

881
01:01:44,200 --> 01:01:45,702
DOCTOR TANUMA

882
01:01:45,785 --> 01:01:48,496
Tanuma? Her name's Numata. Idiots.

883
01:01:53,668 --> 01:01:56,170
TOHYAMA COSMETIC SURGERY CLINIC

884
01:02:35,042 --> 01:02:36,544
Hey, Macky! What's up?

885
01:02:36,627 --> 01:02:38,337
What are you doing here?

886
01:02:39,380 --> 01:02:42,592
Just walking by, you know.
Just figured I'd say hi.

887
01:02:43,885 --> 01:02:45,428
See how you were doing.

888
01:03:23,007 --> 01:03:24,133
<i>I mean it.</i>

889
01:03:25,301 --> 01:03:27,970
<i>It was truly</i>
<i>the work of my successor, Rin.</i>
